      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Cincinnati, Lebanon and Northern Railway began running through Deer Park in 1881, linking the town to regional trade routes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Park%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Deer Park was officially incorporated as a city in 1912, shifting from a rural settlement to an incorporated municipality.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Park%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1894 the town already had a single store and a Catholic church, showing its modest but growing infrastructure.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer_Park%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Deer Park lies in Hamilton County and is considered a suburb of Cincinnati, tying it to the larger metropolitan area.",
